# Line endings: LF in the repository and LF in every checkout.
#
# The repository is authored with LF, and three of its gates depend on the
# working tree carrying exactly the bytes the index holds: prettier
# (endOfLine lf) reports every CRLF file as unformatted, node:test's
# brand-assets suite hashes assets/fonts/OFL.txt against the design
# package manifest, and the ratification tooling digests files. On a
# Windows machine with the Git for Windows default core.autocrlf=true, a
# plain clone checked out 306 text files as CRLF, so `format:check`
# failed on 248 files and the font-notice digest test failed while the
# committed content was correct (find 53, 2026-09-28, Kody's desktop).
# `eol=lf` makes the checkout independent of that machine setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary by extension, so no heuristic ever decides for them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.p12 binary
